{"by":"LetThingsBeDiff","descendants":122,"id":50583761,"kids":[50585622,50587032,50586963,50586237,50586760,50586242,50586387,50585827,50586773,50586861,50586724,50586427,50585933,50584426,50584290,50586897,50586901,50586447,50585352,50586546,50584056,50586637,50586458,50584146,50586871,50587098,50584608,50584872,50586416,50586163,50586437,50585422,50586825,50586987,50585198,50584116,50584243,50586451,50583934,50585628,50584405,50586611,50586448,50585453,50585262,50586286,50586347,50586453,50584456,50583970,50584139,50586795,50584700],"score":128,"text":"I&#x27;m Senior software engineer in the US (DMV area), with 15y of experience. Worked for Fortune 50+ company and bunch of mid-size companies. Been unemployed for 2y and can&#x27;t find a job, within those 2 years, I pretty much spent my savings that I&#x27;ve saved through years, maybe have 4-5 months left to support my household. Currently, I tutor math and probably about to start working as manager in pizzaria.<p>In Jan 2025, I quit from a mid-size insurance tech company(1000+) after working there for almost 4y, because I was tipped off the they were about to start layoffs and they did. Well, since then I have zero luck finding any job in SWE.<p>At this point, I have massive gap in my resume that I can&#x27;t explain to recruiters, I can still code (C#&#x2F;.NET&#x2F;AWS) and learned the AI, but who cares if date of my last employment is Jan2025. What should I do ?<p>If you have an alternative path (something completely different from SWE or SWE adjacent) that pays &quot;well&quot;, I would like to hear.","time":1795216712,"title":"Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?","type":"story"}
